\section*{1. Executive Summary}
UPAS-X is a high-precision, massively parallel astrophysical simulation engine designed to model multi-body shadow geometry, relativistic ephemerides, HDR flux attenuation, and dynamic BVH spatial partitioning. This packet provides the complete scientific validation framework, empirical benchmarks, reproducibility artifacts, and stability analyses required for independent peer review.

\section*{2. System Description}

\subsection*{2.1 Core Capabilities}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Multi-body shadow geometry: Umbra, Penumbra, Antumbra, Annular zones.
    \item HDR flux attenuation modeling across dense stellar fields.
    \item Relativistic ephemeris integration with PPN corrections.
    \item Dynamic BVH spatial partitioning with SAH-based GPU refit kernels.
    \item CUDA-accelerated ray--cone intersection for U/P/A boundary surfaces.
    \item MPI-distributed spatial tensor computation for $>10^9$ active nodes.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{2.2 Hardware Platform}
\begin{itemize}
    \item 16 enterprise compute nodes.
    \item 128 NVIDIA H100 GPUs (80GB HBM3 each).
    \item NVSwitch + NVLink 4.0 fabric.
    \item Dual AMD EPYC 9654 CPUs per node.
    \item 1.5 TB DDR5-4800 RAM per node.
    \item HDR InfiniBand (400 Gb/s) interconnect.
\end{itemize}

\section*{3. Scientific Validation Framework}

\subsection*{3.1 Numerical Validation}

\subsubsection*{Integrator Accuracy}
\begin{itemize}
    \item 15th-order RKN symplectic integrator.
    \item Hamiltonian drift constraint:
    \[
        \left| \frac{H(t)-H(0)}{H(0)} \right| < 10^{-10}.
    \]
    \item Validation against analytic two-body and three-body solutions.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{BVH and Ray--Cone Geometry}
\begin{itemize}
    \item SAH-based BVH construction validated against brute-force intersection.
    \item Cone boundary correctness validated against analytic geometry.
    \item Condition number monitoring:
    \[
        \kappa = \|A\| \cdot \|A^{-1}\|.
    \]
\end{itemize}

